For \(|x| \leq 2\), \(\max\{|x|,x^{2}\}\) has corners at \(x = 0\) and \(x = \pm 1\). At \(x = \pm 2\), the slope changes from \(\pm 4\) to \(\mp 2\). Thus \(f\) is not differentiable at the \(5\) points \(\{ - 2, - 1,0,1,2\}\).
{{figure}}
Hence the answer is (B).

JM20190112253.t:
The equation \(|z_{1}| = 9\) represents a circle centered at \(O(0,0)\) with radius \(r_{1} = 9\). The equation \(|z_{2} - (3 + 4i)| = 4\) represents a circle centered at \(C(3,4)\) with radius \(r_{2} = 4\). The distance between their centres is \(OC = \sqrt{3^{2} + 4^{2}} = 5 = r_{1} - r_{2}\), so the two circles touch each other internally. Hence they share a common point, and the minimum value of \(|z_{1} - z_{2}|\) is \(0\).
{{figure}}
Hence the answer is (A).

JM201904101P54.t:
The inequalities \(- 2 \leq x - y \leq 2\) and \(- 2 \leq x + y \leq 2\) form a square with vertices \((2,0),(0,2),( - 2,0),(0, - 2)\), whose side length is \(\sqrt{2^{2} + 2^{2}} = 2\sqrt{2}\) units.
{{figure}}
Hence the answer is (B).

JM201901121P74.t:
On \(y^{2} = 4x\), \(P(4, - 4)\) has parameter \(t_{1} = - 2\) and \(Q(9,6)\) has \(t_{2} = 3\). For \(X(t^{2},2t)\) on arc \(POQ\), \(\text{Area}( \bigtriangleup PXQ)\) is maximized when the tangent at \(X\) is parallel to \(PQ\), i.e., \(t = \frac{t_{1} + t_{2}}{2} = \frac{1}{2}\), giving \(X\left(\frac{1}{4},1\right)\) and maximum area \(\frac{125}{4}\) sq. units.
{{figure}}
Hence the answer is (B).

JM201901121P75.t:
Let the top-right vertex of the rectangle be \((x,12 - x^{2})\) with \(0 < x < \sqrt{12}\). The area is \(A(x) = 2x(12 - x^{2}) = 24x - 2x^{3}\). Setting \(A'(x) = 24 - 6x^{2} = 0 \Rightarrow x = 2\), which gives maximum area \(A(2) = 4(12 - 4) = 32\).
{{figure}}
Hence the answer is (D).

JM201904092P107.t:
The side joining \(A( - 8,5)\) and \(B(6,5)\) is horizontal of length \(14\), and its perpendicular bisector is \(x = - 1\). The centre of the circle is the intersection of \(x = - 1\) and the diameter \(3y = x + 7\), which is \(C( - 1,2)\). Since \(C\) has \(y\)-coordinate \(2\), the other horizontal side of the rectangle lies at \(y = 2 - (5 - 2) = - 1\), so the height is \(5 - ( - 1) = 6\). Area \(= 14 \times 6 = 84\).
{{figure}}
Hence the answer is (B).

