Here \(C_{1} = (1,1)\) with \(r_{1} = 2\), and \(C_{2} = (3,3)\) with \(r_{2} = 2\). Since \(C_{1}C_{2} = \sqrt{4 + 4} = 2\sqrt{2}\) and \(r_{1}^{2} + r_{2}^{2} = 8 = (C_{1}C_{2})^{2}\), the two circles are orthogonal (\(\angle C_{1}PC_{2} = 90^{\circ}\)). Thus the area of quadrilateral \(PC_{1}QC_{2}\) is \(2 \times \frac{1}{2}r_{1}r_{2} = 2 \times 2 = 4\).
